Type: recovered correspondence
Participants: Oscar Lindström, Grant Holloway

Oscar Lindström:
Grant, tell me that's not you in the photo.

Grant Holloway:
What photo?

Oscar Lindström:
Half the net is talking about the naked party on Vesta Ring Station. The photo leaked from the party.

Grant Holloway:
No, not me. But that idiot is one of ours.

Oscar Lindström:
Half-assed posers and show-offs.

Oscar Lindström:
They should be training, considering everyone's losing their minds right now. And they're out having fun.

Grant Holloway:
That's exactly why they're having fun. They're heading into the unknown. You can understand that.

Oscar Lindström:
That's not an excuse. They're not on vacation. How did you even let this happen?

Grant Holloway:
He's not from my unit. And I'm not his mother. My guys are responsible.

Oscar Lindström:
Looks like you people at the Club decided to become media personalities. New generation contractors. By day, meatheads escorting questionable cargo. By night, half-naked clowns on a luxury deck getting caught in someone else's stories.

Grant Holloway:
It was a closed event. Phones were taken at the entrance.

Oscar Lindström:
Right. Which is why I'm currently looking at you people from three different angles.

Grant Holloway:
Quit grumbling. Nobody there will recognize him except you and me.

Oscar Lindström:
And the journalists. The article mentions people from mercenary companies being present.

Grant Holloway:
Did you write just to gloat?

Oscar Lindström:
No. I wrote because there's a table in one of the photos. And there are cans on that table.

Grant Holloway:
And?

Oscar Lindström:
You don't recognize the can?

Grant Holloway:
If you mean Drop Shot, that's just a regular energy drink.

Oscar Lindström:
Regular Drop Shot is orange. The one in the photo is Redline. Black stripe, red cap, small marking near the bottom of the can. Don't pretend you don't know. They pushed that stuff on every soldier and everyone around them.

Grant Holloway:
Well, maybe he wanted to recharge a little. Looks like the guy got tired.

Oscar Lindström:
Then what the hell did he need a combat psychostimulant for? Was he planning to fuck half the station? His dick would fall off first. Or his heart would stop.

Grant Holloway:
You talk like you've never used anything like that yourself.

Oscar Lindström:
I have. Of course I have. I'm not pretending to be a saint. When your squad is in deep shit, your medic is face down in the dirt, and you still need to hold the sector for another three hours, you'll try worse things than that. But I never brought that shit to a brothel.

Oscar Lindström:
There's a difference between doing the job and dancing naked while waving your dick around. He's making all of us look like a joke.

Grant Holloway:
Don't worry, he already got his ass handed to him. They wanted to shove a railgun slug up him, but they showed mercy. Now he's just washing everyone's pants.

Oscar Lindström:
Better have him strip and oil weapons. Clean pants won't help in a fight.

Grant Holloway:
Oscar.

Oscar Lindström:
What?

Grant Holloway:
Will this blow over?

Oscar Lindström:
The news? Yes. In a week they'll find someone dumber and everyone will forget. The important thing is that the screw-up doesn't forget.

Grant Holloway:
Do you think they can connect him to us?

Oscar Lindström:
Nah, probably not. Everyone who recognized him doesn't give a shit. If you're worried about the journalists, don't. Nobody's going to tell them.

Grant Holloway:
If anyone asks you, can you keep quiet? We don't really want to ruin our reputation.

Oscar Lindström:
Don't worry. I'll say they were randoms or ex-contractors. Worst case, you fire him retroactively and say he wasn't yours.

Grant Holloway:
Thanks.

Oscar Lindström:
Don't thank me. And he's not the first contractor who thought "closed party" meant there wouldn't be cameras.

Grant Holloway:
Can Redline become a problem?

Oscar Lindström:
Redline is already a problem. If someone proves you're dragging field stims into civilian parties, the questions won't stop with you. They'll go to the supplier, to whoever let it onto the station, and to whoever decided it was normal party dressing for rich idiots.

Grant Holloway:
Very funny.

Oscar Lindström:
I'm not laughing. You look like people who were given money, weapons, and zero upbringing.

Grant Holloway:
Are you done?

Oscar Lindström:
Yes. Keep quiet. And next time you people want to feel like stars, hire actors. At least that's their actual job.